                    AwakeningSection(heading: "The Problem", body: "Every day, billions of dollars are spent engineering what you believe.\n\nNot informing you. ENGINEERING your beliefs. There's a difference.\n\nInformation says: \"Here are the facts. Draw your own conclusion.\"\nEngineered narrative says: \"Here's what to feel, who to blame, and what to do — and if you question it, you're the problem.\"\n\nEdward Bernays — Sigmund Freud's nephew — wrote the playbook in 1928. His book \"Propaganda\" literally opens with: \"The conscious and intelligent manipulation of the organized habits and opinions of the masses is an important element in democratic society.\"\n\nHe wasn't hiding it. He was bragging.\n\nSince then, the tools have gotten exponentially more sophisticated. Social media algorithms, 24/7 news cycles, synthetic media, astroturfed movements, controlled opposition — the manipulation stack in 2026 makes Bernays look like a kid with crayons.\n\nAnd your brain? Your brain is running the same hardware it had 200,000 years ago. Tribal wiring. Threat detection. Authority deference. Emotional override. Every single vulnerability that kept your ancestors alive on the savanna is now being exploited to control what you think, buy, vote for, and fear.\n\nYou can't fix this with willpower. You can't fix it by \"being smarter.\" You need a SYSTEM."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "What ERSS Is", body: "The Engineer Reality Scoring System is a structured, repeatable protocol for scoring the manipulation likelihood of ANY narrative — news story, policy announcement, social media trend, historical event, advertisement, or future scenario.\n\nIt uses 8 weighted indicators scored 0-12.5 each, producing a total score from 0-100.\n\n0-25: Low manipulation risk. Probably organic information.\n26-50: Moderate. Worth cross-checking independently.\n51-75: High. Probable psyop element. Apply deeper analysis.\n76-100: Engineered reality. High-confidence manipulation. Pause ALL action.\n\nThis isn't conspiracy thinking. It's the opposite. Conspiracy thinking is pattern-matching without rigor — seeing manipulation everywhere based on feelings. ERSS is rigorous, scored, and testable. It forces you to show your work.\n\nIf something scores low, accept it. If it scores high, investigate further. If you can't score it cleanly, that itself is data — the narrative may be deliberately ambiguous to resist analysis.\n\nThe goal isn't paranoia. The goal is SOVEREIGNTY. Reclaiming your attention, your emotions, and your decisions from systems designed to hijack them.\n\nStudies on structured checklist-based misinformation detection (Pennycook & Rand meta-analyses; MIT Media Lab) show they outperform gut intuition by 35-60%. Structure beats instinct when the game is rigged."),
