                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Step-by-Step", body: "Run this like a root-cause analysis. Same discipline. Same rigor.\n\nSTEP 1: CAPTURE RAW INPUT (30 seconds)\nSave the headline, screenshot, video clip, or event description. Note the date, source, and platform. Don't analyze yet — just capture.\n\nSTEP 2: RUN ERSS SCORING (5-10 minutes)\nGo through each indicator. Score 0-12.5. Write brief evidence for each score. Don't overthink — first-pass scoring is usually accurate.\n\nSTEP 3: APPLY GROUNDED FILTERS (2 minutes)\nShadow Check: \"Is this triggering my personal projection? Am I seeing this as threatening because of MY shadow, or because it genuinely IS threatening?\"\nQuantum Check: \"Is this context-dependent? Would I score it differently if the source were different?\"\nPredictive Coding Check: \"What prediction error is being amplified? Is my model actually wrong, or is someone exploiting my model's vulnerabilities?\"\n\nSTEP 4: CROSS-VERIFY (5 minutes)\nFind 3 independent sources. Not 3 outlets running the same wire story — 3 genuinely independent perspectives. Map the beneficiaries.\n\nSTEP 5: DECIDE & LOG\nFour options:\n□ Accept as data — Score is low. Information appears organic. File it.\n□ Cross-verify — Score is moderate. Need more data before forming opinion.\n□ Pause & Observe — Score is high. Do NOT act on this emotionally. Watch how the narrative develops over 72 hours.\n□ Counter with facts — Score is very high. You've identified likely manipulation. Share your analysis (not your outrage) with others.\n\nSTEP 6: ITERATE\nAdd every scored event to your personal dataset. Over time, you'll see meta-patterns: which outlets score high consistently, which types of events are most engineered, which of YOUR vulnerabilities get exploited most often.\n\nThat's ERSS. It takes 10 minutes. It turns you from passive consumer into active systems debugger.\n\nThe most powerful version is when you score something you AGREE with. That's where the real work happens. Scoring narratives you disagree with is easy — your bias does the work. Scoring narratives that validate your existing beliefs? That takes integrity."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "The Unity Test", body: "After scoring, always ask one final question:\n\n\"Does accepting this narrative increase division or unity?\"\n\nThis isn't naive. This is the deepest pattern recognition in the entire course.\n\nEvery engineered narrative benefits from division. EVERY one. Because divided people are controllable. United people are not.\n\nIf a story makes you hate a group of humans — any group — that's the biggest red flag of all. Not because the group is innocent. Not because criticism is wrong. But because hate is the most exploitable emotion humans produce, and every power structure in history has used it to maintain control.\n\nThe billionaire doesn't fear the liberal OR the conservative. The billionaire fears the day they stop fighting each other and look up.\n\nThe politician doesn't fear the left OR the right. The politician fears the day both sides realize they're being played by the same game.\n\nTribal division is the oldest psyop on Earth. And it still works because it hijacks wiring that's 200,000 years old.\n\nERSS helps you see through it. Not by making you suspicious of everything — but by giving you a structured way to separate signal from noise, information from manipulation, and genuine threat from manufactured fear.\n\nSee clearly. Think clearly. Choose freely. That's Aperture."),
