                emoji: "📈",
                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Historical Calibration", body: "To trust the system, you need to calibrate it against known events. Here are examples where the historical record is well-documented:\n\nEXAMPLE: GULF OF TONKIN INCIDENT (1964)\nNarrative: \"North Vietnam attacked US destroyers unprovoked.\"\nResult: Used to justify massive escalation of Vietnam War.\nHistorical truth: Declassified NSA documents (2005) confirmed the second attack never happened.\n\nERSS Score:\n1. Focus Hijack: 11/12.5 — Wall-to-wall coverage, no competing narratives\n2. Authority Inversion: 10/12.5 — President and military speaking definitively without evidence\n3. Tribal Polarization: 9/12.5 — \"Support our troops\" = loyalty test\n4. Emotion Override: 12/12.5 — Pure fear + patriotic rage\n5. Novelty & Timing: 11/12.5 — Perfectly timed for Congressional authorization vote\n6. Context Boundary Shift: 12/12.5 — Tonkin Resolution gave president near-unlimited war power\n7. Follow-the-Money: 10/12.5 — Defense contractors, military-industrial complex\n8. Frame & Fallacies: 10/12.5 — False dilemma, appeal to patriotism, hasty generalization\n\nTOTAL: 85/100 — Engineered Reality\nConfirmed by declassified documents 41 years later.\n\nEXAMPLE: IRAQ WMD (2002-2003)\nNarrative: \"Iraq has weapons of mass destruction. We must act.\"\nResult: Full-scale invasion. Hundreds of thousands of casualties.\nHistorical truth: No WMDs found. Intelligence was cherry-picked and fabricated.\n\nERSS Score: 92/100\nEvery single indicator scored 9+ . The playbook was textbook.\n\nThese aren't conspiracy theories. These are declassified, acknowledged, documented historical events. ERSS would have flagged both in real-time if anyone had been using it."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Practice Framework", body: "YOUR ASSIGNMENT:\n\nPick three events — one from each category:\n\n1. HISTORICAL: Choose any well-documented event you already know the outcome of. Score it. See if ERSS matches the historical record.\n\n2. CURRENT: Choose a narrative that's active RIGHT NOW. Score it. Save the report. Check back in 30-90 days to see how it develops.\n\n3. PERSONAL: Choose a belief you hold strongly. Not a news event — a personal conviction. Score the narrative that gave you that belief. This is the hardest and most valuable exercise.\n\nTips for honest scoring:\n• Score BEFORE you research. Your first-pass intuition, structured through the 8 indicators, is usually more accurate than post-research rationalization.\n• If you can't score an indicator, note \"insufficient data\" — that itself is informative.\n• Pay special attention to Indicator 3 (Tribal Polarization). If a narrative makes you feel contempt for a group of humans, add 2 points to every indicator as a bias correction.\n• Keep a running log. Over weeks, your pattern recognition will sharpen dramatically.\n\nThe goal is not to score everything as a psyop. The goal is to score ACCURATELY. Some events are organic. Some crises are real. Some authorities are legitimate. The system helps you tell the difference — with data instead of paranoia.\n\nCAUTION:\nERSS is probabilistic, not infallible. A high score means \"investigate further,\" not \"this is definitely fake.\" A low score means \"probably organic,\" not \"definitely true.\"\n\nNever weaponize ERSS against individuals. It's designed for narratives and systems, not people. Using it to \"score\" a person's trustworthiness is a misuse of the tool.\n\nAnd if your ERSS scores are consistently above 80 for EVERYTHING you encounter — you may be in a paranoia spiral. That's your shadow projecting threat onto every input. Step back. Ground. Apply the shadow protocol from Module 7. Then return to scoring with fresh eyes."),
